Lab 2 --- Download and install Android Studio
Objective: Install Android Studio and the Android SDK on Windows.
Official download: https://developer.android.com/studio
2.1 Installation
Download the Windows installer from the official Android Developers
website.
Run the installer.
Choose Custom if you want to review the components.
Select Android Studio, Android SDK and Android Virtual
Device/Emulator where offered.
Keep the default SDK path unless storage requires a change.
Accept the SDK licences and allow downloads to complete.
Open Android Studio and confirm the Welcome screen appears.
A common SDK location is:
``` text
C:\Users\<username>\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk
```
Record the actual path shown by Android Studio. Some components are
installed later through SDK Manager rather than the initial wizard.
2.2 SDK Manager
Open More Actions → SDK Manager or Settings → Languages &
Frameworks → Android SDK.
Under SDK Platforms, install a stable platform selected for the
course.
Under SDK Tools, verify:
Android SDK Platform-Tools
Android SDK Build-Tools
Android Emulator
Android SDK Command-line Tools (latest)
Use an Android version supported by the selected training APK. Older
vulnerable apps may not work on the newest Android release.
2.3 Verify tools in PowerShell
Replace the path if your SDK is elsewhere:
``` powershell
$env:ANDROID_HOME = "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Android\Sdk"
$env:Path += ";$env:ANDROID_HOME\platform-tools"
adb version
```
Check emulator:
``` powershell
& "$env:ANDROID_HOME\emulator\emulator.exe" -version
```
Learner task: Record Android Studio version, SDK path, installed
platform/API, Platform-Tools version and Emulator version.
