PART B --- ADB AND KALI CONNECTIVITY
Lab 4 --- Configure Android Debug Bridge
Objective: Establish reliable ADB access to the emulator.
ADB is part of Android SDK Platform-Tools. It supports application
installation, package inspection, log collection and shell interaction.
4.1 Verify ADB on Windows
With the emulator running, open PowerShell:
``` powershell
adb devices -l
```
Expected output resembles:
``` text
List of devices attached
emulator-5554    device
```
If no device appears:
``` powershell
adb kill-server
adb start-server
adb devices -l
```
4.2 Install ADB on Kali if required
``` bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y adb
adb version
```
If it is already installed, record the version.
4.3 Understand two connection patterns
Pattern A --- Windows ADB: Windows ADB controls the local Windows
emulator. Transfer the APK to Kali for analysis. This is the simplest
initial workflow.
Pattern B --- Kali ADB: Kali ADB connects to the Windows-hosted
emulator over a controlled network. This allows Kali commands and
scripts to control the device, but requires a reachable ADB endpoint and
appropriate firewall/network configuration.
Do not assume the emulator ADB port is reachable from another VM by
default.
4.4 Optional ADB TCP connection
On Windows PowerShell, with the emulator connected:
``` powershell
adb devices
adb tcpip 5555
```
Find the Windows address on the network shared with Kali:
``` powershell
ipconfig
```
Use the address belonging to the correct host-only or explicitly
configured adapter.
From Kali:
``` bash
adb connect <WINDOWS_HOST_IP>:5555
adb devices -l
```
Replace the placeholder with the actual reachable address.
If it fails, verify the VirtualBox network mode, routing, Windows
Firewall, ADB listener and selected adapter. Do not expose ADB to a
public or untrusted network. Disable the TCP debugging exposure after
the exercise if it is no longer required.
4.5 Verify shell access
``` bash
adb shell getprop ro.build.version.release
adb shell getprop ro.build.version.sdk
adb shell getprop ro.product.model
adb shell pm list packages
```
Learner task: Demonstrate device connection, OS/API discovery,
package enumeration and ADB shell access. Save the command output.
