Lab 8 --- Permission analysis
Objective: Determine whether permissions are necessary and
proportionate.
8.1 Inspect package permissions
``` bash
adb shell dumpsys package <PACKAGE_NAME>
```
Alternatively, inspect the decoded manifest in Lab 11.
8.2 Permission review table
---
Permission             Possible purpose  Data accessed     Risk if misused
---
INTERNET               Backend           Network data      Data exposure
communication
CAMERA                 Camera feature    Images/video      Privacy impact
RECORD_AUDIO           Audio feature     Microphone        Privacy impact
ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION   Location feature  Precise location  Tracking/privacy
READ_CONTACTS          Contact feature   Address book      Data disclosure
Permissions are not automatically vulnerabilities. Consider business
necessity, runtime controls, data handling and least privilege.
8.3 Inspect runtime permissions
On the emulator:
Open Settings.
Open Apps.
Select the training app.
Open Permissions.
Review allowed and denied permissions.
Compare with manifest declarations.
Learner challenge: Identify two permissions needing a clear business
justification. Explain whether the app could function without them.
