Lab 13 --- Initial insecure storage review
Objective: Identify application storage locations and assess whether
sensitive information may be stored insecurely.
13.1 Understand sandboxing
Explain private app data directories, app UID isolation, shared storage,
debuggable builds and the difference between rooted/test environments
and normal production devices.
13.2 Understand access limitations
``` bash
adb shell pm path <PACKAGE_NAME>
```
On a non-rooted emulator, direct access to `/data/data/<PACKAGE_NAME>`
may be denied. This is expected and should not be treated as a tool
failure.
13.3 Collect logs
``` bash
adb logcat -c
```
Perform a normal test action, then:
``` bash
adb logcat -d > application_log.txt
grep -iE 'password|token|secret|auth|key' application_log.txt
```
Use synthetic values only. Do not collect or publish personal data.
13.4 Review storage APIs in JADX
Search for:
``` text
SharedPreferences
SQLiteDatabase
FileOutputStream
openFileOutput
getExternalFilesDir
getExternalStorageDirectory
```
Learner challenge: Identify one storage mechanism, what data it
stores, where it is stored and what protection is visible in the code.
