Lab 15 --- Mobile network reconnaissance
Objective: Understand application communication behaviour.
15.1 Device network information
``` bash
adb shell ip addr
adb shell ip route
```
15.2 Connectivity test
Use only an approved lab endpoint:
``` bash
adb shell ping -c 4 <APPROVED_TEST_HOST>
```
Some Android images do not include `ping`; use an approved alternative
if necessary.
15.3 Observe application behaviour
Start a clean test session.
Clear old proxy history.
Launch the training application.
Perform one feature at a time.
Record associated requests and responses.
Identify API hostnames and paths.
Note HTTP versus HTTPS.
Record authentication/session mechanisms without copying secrets
into reports.
15.4 Analysis questions
Does the app communicate with expected domains?
Does it use HTTPS?
Are redirects handled safely?
Are tokens sent in appropriate headers?
Are sensitive values placed in URLs?
Does the app expose unnecessary diagnostic endpoints?
Are API responses validated?
Deliverable: Traffic inventory with timestamp, feature, destination
host, method, path, status and security observation. Redact tokens and
personal data.
