Lab 17 --- Wireshark packet analysis
Objective: Correlate application actions with network-level packet
observations.
17.1 Identify interface
``` bash
ip addr
```
Start Wireshark and select the interface carrying the emulator/Kali
traffic.
17.2 Capture
Start capture.
Perform one known app action.
Stop capture.
Save as `mobile_lab_capture.pcapng`.
17.3 Useful display filters
``` text
dns
tcp
tls
http
```
Specific IP:
``` text
ip.addr == <TEST_IP>
```
17.4 Inspect DNS and TLS
Record DNS query/response, response code, TLS Client Hello, visible SNI
where available, TLS version and handshake outcome.
Encrypted payloads are not readable merely because a packet capture
exists.
Learner challenge: Correlate one app action with DNS and TCP/TLS
traffic. Explain what the capture proves and what it does not prove.
