PART G --- TROUBLESHOOTING
23. Emulator does not start
Check:
Is CPU virtualization enabled in firmware?
Is Windows Hypervisor Platform configured as required by the
installed Emulator?
Does `emulator -accel-check` report acceleration?
Is there enough RAM and disk?
Is the system image compatible?
Are emulator diagnostics available?
Try a cold boot. If necessary, wipe AVD data after preserving evidence.
Do not immediately disable VBS or Memory Integrity.
24. ADB shows no devices
On Windows:
``` powershell
adb kill-server
adb start-server
adb devices -l
```
On Kali:
``` bash
adb kill-server
adb start-server
adb devices -l
```
Ensure the command is using the intended ADB server and the emulator is
running.
25. ADB unauthorized
Unlock the emulator.
Check for debugging authorization prompts.
Reconnect the ADB session.
Restart the ADB server if required.
Avoid deleting ADB keys without a clear reason.
26. APK installation fails
``` bash
adb install -r target.apk
```
Record the full error. Verify APK integrity, minimum SDK, architecture,
signature conflict, storage and split APK requirements.
27. Kali cannot reach Burp
``` bash
ip addr
ip route
```
Verify VirtualBox network mode, host/Kali reachability, listener
binding, firewall, proxy address and port.
28. HTTPS traffic is not visible
Possible causes include proxy misconfiguration, app proxy bypass, user
CA trust restrictions, certificate pinning, custom network stack or no
request being made. Do not label it a pinning issue without evidence.
29. JADX/APKTool output is incomplete
Update from a trusted source.
Verify APK hash.
Check whether the APK is split.
Inspect all DEX files.
Compare tool outputs.
Remember obfuscation and native code can limit reconstruction.
30. Frida cannot attach
Check client/server version compatibility, device ABI, server
execution/permissions, ADB connectivity, process state and emulator/root
constraints. Use official Frida documentation for version-specific
setup.
